{"function_name": "escape", "code_before": "def escape(s):\n    s = s.replace(\"&\", \"&amp;\")  # Must be done first!\n    s = s.replace(\"<\", \"&lt;\")\n    s = s.replace(\">\", \"&gt;\")\n\n    return s\n", "code_after": "", "commit_message": "Fix XSS in some dashboards queries (#2785)\n\n* prevent xss on time range text fields\r\n\r\n* prevent xss on dashbord queries", "commit": "https://github.com/graphite-project/graphite-web/commit/2f178f490e10efc03cd1d27c72f64ecab224eb23", "description": "A vulnerability was found in Graphite Web. It has been classified as problematic. Affected is an unknown function of the component Absolute Time Range Handler. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The name of the patch is 2f178f490e10efc03cd1d27c72f64ecab224eb23. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-216744.", "file_change_id": 122790017806683, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-m973-4vpc-x43c", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "handleInputParameterError", "code_before": "def handleInputParameterError(f):\n    def new_f(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return f(*args, **kwargs)\n        except InputParameterError as e:\n            msgStr = str(e)\n            log.warning('%s', msgStr)\n            return HttpResponseBadRequest(escape(msgStr))\n\n    return new_f\n", "code_after": "def handleInputParameterError(f):\n    def new_f(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return f(*args, **kwargs)\n        except InputParameterError as e:\n            msgStr = str(e)\n            log.warning('%s', msgStr)\n            return HttpResponseBadRequest(htmlEscape(msgStr))\n\n    return new_f\n"}, {"function_name": "handleInputParameterError.new_f", "code_before": "    def new_f(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return f(*args, **kwargs)\n        except InputParameterError as e:\n            msgStr = str(e)\n            log.warning('%s', msgStr)\n            return HttpResponseBadRequest(escape(msgStr))\n", "code_after": "    def new_f(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return f(*args, **kwargs)\n        except InputParameterError as e:\n            msgStr = str(e)\n            log.warning('%s', msgStr)\n            return HttpResponseBadRequest(htmlEscape(msgStr))\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `escape` was removed in the commit. The commit message and the vulnerability description suggest that the commit is intended to fix a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the Graphite Web project.\n\nThe `escape` function was used to replace certain characters in a string with their corresponding HTML entities, which is a common way to prevent XSS attacks. However, the function was removed in the commit, and it seems that it was replaced by a function called `htmlEscape` in other parts of the code.\n\nGiven that the `escape` function was removed and replaced with `htmlEscape` in the context of an XSS fix, it's reasonable to infer that the `escape` function was part of the vulnerability. Therefore, the answer is 1, the function is vulnerable.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "title", "code_before": "    def title(self):\n        if base_hasattr(self.context, 'get_full_title'):\n            title = self.context.get_full_title()\n        else:\n            title = self.context.Title()\n        title = title and safe_unicode(title) or u\"\"\n        return title\n", "code_after": "    def title(self):\n        if base_hasattr(self.context, 'get_full_title'):\n            title = self.context.get_full_title()\n        else:\n            title = self.context.Title()\n        title = title and safe_unicode(title) or u\"\"\n        return escape(title, quote=True)\n", "commit_message": "Escaped term-contact viewlet title special chars to avoid xss", "commit": "https://github.com/collective/collective.contact.widget/commit/5da36305ca7ed433782be8901c47387406fcda12", "description": "collective.contact.widget is an add-on is part of the collective.contact.* suite. A vulnerability classified as problematic was found in collective.contact.widget up to 1.12. This vulnerability affects the function title of the file src/collective/contact/widget/widgets.py. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. The attack can be initiated remotely. The name of the patch is 5da36305ca7ed433782be8901c47387406fcda12. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-216496.", "file_change_id": 97196419232544, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5pqf-rvm7-3wgw", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `title` in the file `src/collective/contact/widget/widgets.py` was vulnerable to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack. The vulnerability was classified as problematic and could be initiated remotely.\n\nThe change in the function `title` is the addition of the `escape(title, quote=True)` function call. This function is typically used to replace special characters in strings with their HTML-safe equivalents, which is a common way to prevent XSS attacks. \n\nThe commit message \"Escaped term-contact viewlet title special chars to avoid xss\" further confirms that this change was made to fix the XSS vulnerability. \n\nTherefore, the function `title` was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "renderCell", "code_before": "    def renderCell(self, value):\n        username = getattr(value, self.field, '')\n        if username and username != EMPTY_STRING:\n            member = api.user.get(username)\n            return member.getUser().getProperty('fullname').decode('utf-8')\n\n        return \"\"\n", "code_after": "    def renderCell(self, value):\n        username = getattr(value, self.field, '')\n        if username and username != EMPTY_STRING:\n            member = api.user.get(username)\n            return escape(member.getUser().getProperty('fullname').decode('utf-8'))\n\n        return \"\"\n", "commit_message": "Escaped some column rendering to avoid xss", "commit": "https://github.com/collective/collective.task/commit/1aac7f83fa2c2b41d59ba02748912953461f3fac", "description": "A vulnerability was found in collective.task up to 3.0.9. It has been classified as problematic. This affects the function renderCell/AssignedGroupColumn of the file src/collective/task/browser/table.py. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. Upgrading to version 3.0.10 is able to address this issue. The name of the patch is 1aac7f83fa2c2b41d59ba02748912953461f3fac. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component. The associated identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-215907.", "file_change_id": 108635345776449, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4r9h-x77w-mffv", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `renderCell` was indeed vulnerable to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack. The vulnerability was due to the fact that the function was rendering user input (in this case, a username) without properly escaping it, which could allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts.\n\nIn the \"code_after\" section, we can see that the function has been modified to include the `escape` function when rendering the username. This function is used to replace any potentially harmful characters with their safe equivalents, thus preventing any scripts from being executed.\n\nThe commit message \"Escaped some column rendering to avoid xss\" further confirms that this change was made to fix the XSS vulnerability. Therefore, the function `renderCell` was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\nThe answer in JSON format would be:\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "renderCell", "code_before": "    def renderCell(self, item):\n        value = get_value(item, self.attribute, default=())\n\n        if not isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\n            value = (value,)\n\n        gtool = getToolByName(plone.api.portal.get(), 'portal_groups')\n        mtool = getToolByName(plone.api.portal.get(), 'portal_membership')\n        principals = []\n        for principal_id in value:\n            user = mtool.getMemberById(principal_id)\n            if user is not None:\n                principals.append(user.getProperty('fullname', None) or user.getId())\n            else:\n                group = gtool.getGroupById(principal_id)\n                if group is not None:\n                    principals.append(group.getProperty('title', None) or group.getId())\n\n        return ', '.join(principals).decode('utf-8')\n", "code_after": "    def renderCell(self, item):\n        value = get_value(item, self.attribute, default=())\n\n        if not isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\n            value = (value,)\n\n        gtool = getToolByName(plone.api.portal.get(), 'portal_groups')\n        mtool = getToolByName(plone.api.portal.get(), 'portal_membership')\n        principals = []\n        for principal_id in value:\n            user = mtool.getMemberById(principal_id)\n            if user is not None:\n                principals.append(escape(user.getProperty('fullname', None)) or user.getId())\n            else:\n                group = gtool.getGroupById(principal_id)\n                if group is not None:\n                    principals.append(escape(group.getProperty('title', None)) or group.getId())\n\n        return ', '.join(principals).decode('utf-8')\n", "commit_message": "Updated columns to work with z3c.table 2.2. Escaped rendering special caracters to avoid xss", "commit": "https://github.com/collective/collective.dms.basecontent/commit/6c4d616fcc771822a14ebae5e23f3f6d96d134bd", "description": "A vulnerability, which was classified as problematic, has been found in collective.dms.basecontent. This issue affects the function renderCell of the file src/collective/dms/basecontent/browser/column.py. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. The attack may be initiated remotely. Upgrading to version 1.7 or later will address this issue. The patch is at commit 6c4d616fcc771822a14ebae5e23f3f6d96d134bd. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component. The identifier VDB-215813 was assigned to this vulnerability.", "file_change_id": 75195846413440, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r48c-4vfj-h426", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "getLinkContent", "code_before": "    def getLinkContent(self, item):\n        title = get_value(item, 'Title')\n        if isinstance(title, unicode):\n            return title\n        else:\n            return unicode(title, 'utf-8', 'ignore')\n", "code_after": "    def getLinkContent(self, item):\n        title = get_value(item, 'Title')\n        return escape(safe_unicode(title))\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `renderCell` was indeed vulnerable to a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack. The vulnerability was due to the lack of proper escaping of special characters in the user and group properties, which could lead to the execution of malicious scripts if these properties contained such scripts.\n\nIn the `code_after` snippet, we can see that the `escape` function is now being used to sanitize the user and group properties before they are appended to the `principals` list. This change directly addresses the XSS vulnerability by ensuring that any special characters in these properties are properly escaped, thus preventing the execution of any potential scripts.\n\nThe commit message also confirms this, stating that special characters are now escaped to avoid XSS. Therefore, the function `renderCell` was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "_present_feedback", "code_before": "    def _present_feedback(feedback_messages):\n        \"\"\"\n        Transforms feedback messages into format expected by frontend code\n        \"\"\"\n        return [\n            {\"message\": msg.message, \"message_class\": msg.message_class}\n            for msg in feedback_messages\n            if msg.message\n        ]\n", "code_after": "    def _present_feedback(feedback_messages):\n        \"\"\"\n        Transforms feedback messages into format expected by frontend code\n        \"\"\"\n        return [\n            {\"message\": sanitize_html(msg.message), \"message_class\": msg.message_class}\n            for msg in feedback_messages\n            if msg.message\n        ]\n", "commit_message": "feat!: sanitize HTML tags to prevent XSS vulnerabilities\n\nThis allows rendering only a pre-defined set of HTML tags and their attributes.\n\nIt also escapes all HTML code in the zone preview inside the Studio editor.\nAn alternative could be sanitizing this data with `bleach` before passing it\nto the Studio editor (i.e. in the `studio_view`). This would provide a\nconsistent experience between the rendered XBlock and this preview. However,\nthis would lead to overwriting existing data - i.e. when a course author\nsubmits the XBlock, the sanitized data will replace the one from the XBlock\nfield (which has the `Scope.settings` scope). Therefore, we decided to just\nescape the HTML with `Handlebars.Utils.escapeExpression` in the preview.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: disallowed HTML tags (e.g. `<script>`) will no longer be\nrendered in LMS and Studio.", "commit": "https://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/commit/53c4482f9bb6d8c7ccdf5253bd82c84a222b2492", "description": "### Impact\nXSS Vulnerability in multiple XBlock Fields.  Any platform that has deployed the XBlock will be impacted.\n\n### Patches\nhttps://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/commit/53c4482f9bb6d8c7ccdf5253bd82c84a222b2492\n\nThe fix is compatible with all Open edX releases newer than Lilac.\n\n### Workarounds\nNone.\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/pull/295#issuecomment-1277693864\n", "file_change_id": 127298014902336, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qv6c-367r-3w6q", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "show_answer", "code_before": "    def show_answer(self, data, suffix=''):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns correct answer in assessment mode.\n\n        Raises:\n             * JsonHandlerError with 400 error code in standard mode.\n             * JsonHandlerError with 409 error code if the answer is unavailable.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.mode != Constants.ASSESSMENT_MODE:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                400,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"show_answer handler should only be called for assessment mode\")\n            )\n        if not self.is_answer_available:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                409,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"The answer is unavailable\")\n            )\n\n        answer = self._get_correct_state()\n\n        if explanation := self.data.get('explanation', '').strip():\n            if replace_urls_service := self.runtime.service(self, 'replace_urls'):\n                explanation = replace_urls_service.replace_urls(explanation)\n\n            # pylint: disable=fixme\n            # TODO: No longer needed after Maple.\n            else:\n                try:\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_course_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_jump_to_id_urls(explanation)\n                except (TypeError, AttributeError):\n                    logger.debug('Unable to perform URL substitution on the explanation: %s', explanation)\n\n            answer['explanation'] = explanation\n        return answer\n", "code_after": "    def show_answer(self, data, suffix=''):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns correct answer in assessment mode.\n\n        Raises:\n             * JsonHandlerError with 400 error code in standard mode.\n             * JsonHandlerError with 409 error code if the answer is unavailable.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.mode != Constants.ASSESSMENT_MODE:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                400,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"show_answer handler should only be called for assessment mode\")\n            )\n        if not self.is_answer_available:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                409,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"The answer is unavailable\")\n            )\n\n        answer = self._get_correct_state()\n\n        if explanation := self.data.get('explanation', '').strip():\n            if replace_urls_service := self.runtime.service(self, 'replace_urls'):\n                explanation = replace_urls_service.replace_urls(explanation)\n\n            # pylint: disable=fixme\n            # TODO: No longer needed after Maple.\n            else:\n                try:\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_course_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_jump_to_id_urls(explanation)\n                except (TypeError, AttributeError):\n                    logger.debug('Unable to perform URL substitution on the explanation: %s', explanation)\n\n            answer['explanation'] = sanitize_html(explanation)\n        return answer\n"}, {"function_name": "student_view_data", "code_before": "    def student_view_data(self, context=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get the configuration data for the student_view.\n        The configuration is all the settings defined by the author, except for correct answers\n        and feedback.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n            return items\n\n        return {\n            \"block_id\": six.text_type(self.scope_ids.usage_id),\n            \"display_name\": self.display_name,\n            \"type\": self.CATEGORY,\n            \"weight\": self.weight,\n            \"mode\": self.mode,\n            \"zones\": self.zones,\n            \"max_attempts\": self.max_attempts,\n            \"graded\": getattr(self, 'graded', False),\n            \"weighted_max_score\": self.max_score() * self.weight,\n            \"max_items_per_zone\": self.max_items_per_zone,\n            # SDK doesn't supply url_name.\n            \"url_name\": getattr(self, 'url_name', ''),\n            \"display_zone_labels\": self.data.get('displayLabels', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders\": self.data.get('displayBorders', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders_dragging\": self.data.get('displayBordersDragging', False),\n            \"items\": items_without_answers(),\n            \"title\": self.display_name,\n            \"show_title\": self.show_title,\n            \"problem_text\": self.question_text,\n            \"show_problem_header\": self.show_question_header,\n            \"target_img_expanded_url\": self.target_img_expanded_url,\n            \"target_img_description\": self.target_img_description,\n            \"item_background_color\": self.item_background_color or None,\n            \"item_text_color\": self.item_text_color or None,\n            \"has_deadline_passed\": self.has_submission_deadline_passed,\n            \"answer_available\": self.is_answer_available,\n            # final feedback (data.feedback.finish) is not included - it may give away answers.\n        }\n", "code_after": "    def student_view_data(self, context=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get the configuration data for the student_view.\n        The configuration is all the settings defined by the author, except for correct answers\n        and feedback.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n                item['displayName'] = sanitize_html(item.get('displayName', ''))\n            return items\n\n        return {\n            \"block_id\": six.text_type(self.scope_ids.usage_id),\n            \"display_name\": sanitize_html(self.display_name),\n            \"type\": self.CATEGORY,\n            \"weight\": self.weight,\n            \"mode\": self.mode,\n            \"zones\": self.zones,\n            \"max_attempts\": self.max_attempts,\n            \"graded\": getattr(self, 'graded', False),\n            \"weighted_max_score\": self.max_score() * self.weight,\n            \"max_items_per_zone\": self.max_items_per_zone,\n            # SDK doesn't supply url_name.\n            \"url_name\": getattr(self, 'url_name', ''),\n            \"display_zone_labels\": self.data.get('displayLabels', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders\": self.data.get('displayBorders', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders_dragging\": self.data.get('displayBordersDragging', False),\n            \"items\": items_without_answers(),\n            \"title\": sanitize_html(self.display_name),\n            \"show_title\": self.show_title,\n            \"problem_text\": sanitize_html(self.question_text),\n            \"show_problem_header\": self.show_question_header,\n            \"target_img_expanded_url\": self.target_img_expanded_url,\n            \"target_img_description\": self.target_img_description,\n            \"item_background_color\": self.item_background_color or None,\n            \"item_text_color\": self.item_text_color or None,\n            \"has_deadline_passed\": self.has_submission_deadline_passed,\n            \"answer_available\": self.is_answer_available,\n            # final feedback (data.feedback.finish) is not included - it may give away answers.\n        }\n"}, {"function_name": "student_view_data.items_without_answers", "code_before": "        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n            return items\n", "code_after": "        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n                item['displayName'] = sanitize_html(item.get('displayName', ''))\n            return items\n"}, {"function_name": "zones", "code_before": "    def zones(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get drop zone data, defined by the author.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert zone data from old to new format if necessary\n        migrator = StateMigration(self)\n        return [migrator.apply_zone_migrations(zone) for zone in self.data.get('zones', [])]\n", "code_after": "    def zones(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get drop zone data, defined by the author.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert zone data from old to new format if necessary\n        migrator = StateMigration(self)\n        migrated_zones = []\n\n        for zone in self.data.get('zones', []):\n            result = migrator.apply_zone_migrations(zone)\n            result['title'] = sanitize_html(result.get('title', ''))\n            migrated_zones.append(result)\n\n        return migrated_zones\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the vulnerability was an XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) vulnerability in multiple XBlock Fields. The commit message indicates that the fix involves sanitizing HTML tags to prevent XSS vulnerabilities.\n\nLooking at the changes in the \"_present_feedback\" function, it's clear that the function was modified to sanitize the feedback messages. The \"sanitize_html\" function is used to sanitize the 'message' field of the feedback messages. This change is directly related to the vulnerability, as it prevents the execution of potentially malicious scripts that could be embedded in the feedback messages.\n\nTherefore, the \"_present_feedback\" function was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "student_view_data", "code_before": "    def student_view_data(self, context=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get the configuration data for the student_view.\n        The configuration is all the settings defined by the author, except for correct answers\n        and feedback.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n            return items\n\n        return {\n            \"block_id\": six.text_type(self.scope_ids.usage_id),\n            \"display_name\": self.display_name,\n            \"type\": self.CATEGORY,\n            \"weight\": self.weight,\n            \"mode\": self.mode,\n            \"zones\": self.zones,\n            \"max_attempts\": self.max_attempts,\n            \"graded\": getattr(self, 'graded', False),\n            \"weighted_max_score\": self.max_score() * self.weight,\n            \"max_items_per_zone\": self.max_items_per_zone,\n            # SDK doesn't supply url_name.\n            \"url_name\": getattr(self, 'url_name', ''),\n            \"display_zone_labels\": self.data.get('displayLabels', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders\": self.data.get('displayBorders', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders_dragging\": self.data.get('displayBordersDragging', False),\n            \"items\": items_without_answers(),\n            \"title\": self.display_name,\n            \"show_title\": self.show_title,\n            \"problem_text\": self.question_text,\n            \"show_problem_header\": self.show_question_header,\n            \"target_img_expanded_url\": self.target_img_expanded_url,\n            \"target_img_description\": self.target_img_description,\n            \"item_background_color\": self.item_background_color or None,\n            \"item_text_color\": self.item_text_color or None,\n            \"has_deadline_passed\": self.has_submission_deadline_passed,\n            \"answer_available\": self.is_answer_available,\n            # final feedback (data.feedback.finish) is not included - it may give away answers.\n        }\n", "code_after": "    def student_view_data(self, context=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get the configuration data for the student_view.\n        The configuration is all the settings defined by the author, except for correct answers\n        and feedback.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n                item['displayName'] = sanitize_html(item.get('displayName', ''))\n            return items\n\n        return {\n            \"block_id\": six.text_type(self.scope_ids.usage_id),\n            \"display_name\": sanitize_html(self.display_name),\n            \"type\": self.CATEGORY,\n            \"weight\": self.weight,\n            \"mode\": self.mode,\n            \"zones\": self.zones,\n            \"max_attempts\": self.max_attempts,\n            \"graded\": getattr(self, 'graded', False),\n            \"weighted_max_score\": self.max_score() * self.weight,\n            \"max_items_per_zone\": self.max_items_per_zone,\n            # SDK doesn't supply url_name.\n            \"url_name\": getattr(self, 'url_name', ''),\n            \"display_zone_labels\": self.data.get('displayLabels', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders\": self.data.get('displayBorders', False),\n            \"display_zone_borders_dragging\": self.data.get('displayBordersDragging', False),\n            \"items\": items_without_answers(),\n            \"title\": sanitize_html(self.display_name),\n            \"show_title\": self.show_title,\n            \"problem_text\": sanitize_html(self.question_text),\n            \"show_problem_header\": self.show_question_header,\n            \"target_img_expanded_url\": self.target_img_expanded_url,\n            \"target_img_description\": self.target_img_description,\n            \"item_background_color\": self.item_background_color or None,\n            \"item_text_color\": self.item_text_color or None,\n            \"has_deadline_passed\": self.has_submission_deadline_passed,\n            \"answer_available\": self.is_answer_available,\n            # final feedback (data.feedback.finish) is not included - it may give away answers.\n        }\n", "commit_message": "feat!: sanitize HTML tags to prevent XSS vulnerabilities\n\nThis allows rendering only a pre-defined set of HTML tags and their attributes.\n\nIt also escapes all HTML code in the zone preview inside the Studio editor.\nAn alternative could be sanitizing this data with `bleach` before passing it\nto the Studio editor (i.e. in the `studio_view`). This would provide a\nconsistent experience between the rendered XBlock and this preview. However,\nthis would lead to overwriting existing data - i.e. when a course author\nsubmits the XBlock, the sanitized data will replace the one from the XBlock\nfield (which has the `Scope.settings` scope). Therefore, we decided to just\nescape the HTML with `Handlebars.Utils.escapeExpression` in the preview.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: disallowed HTML tags (e.g. `<script>`) will no longer be\nrendered in LMS and Studio.", "commit": "https://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/commit/53c4482f9bb6d8c7ccdf5253bd82c84a222b2492", "description": "### Impact\nXSS Vulnerability in multiple XBlock Fields.  Any platform that has deployed the XBlock will be impacted.\n\n### Patches\nhttps://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/commit/53c4482f9bb6d8c7ccdf5253bd82c84a222b2492\n\nThe fix is compatible with all Open edX releases newer than Lilac.\n\n### Workarounds\nNone.\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/openedx/xblock-drag-and-drop-v2/pull/295#issuecomment-1277693864\n", "file_change_id": 127298014902336, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qv6c-367r-3w6q", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "show_answer", "code_before": "    def show_answer(self, data, suffix=''):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns correct answer in assessment mode.\n\n        Raises:\n             * JsonHandlerError with 400 error code in standard mode.\n             * JsonHandlerError with 409 error code if the answer is unavailable.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.mode != Constants.ASSESSMENT_MODE:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                400,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"show_answer handler should only be called for assessment mode\")\n            )\n        if not self.is_answer_available:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                409,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"The answer is unavailable\")\n            )\n\n        answer = self._get_correct_state()\n\n        if explanation := self.data.get('explanation', '').strip():\n            if replace_urls_service := self.runtime.service(self, 'replace_urls'):\n                explanation = replace_urls_service.replace_urls(explanation)\n\n            # pylint: disable=fixme\n            # TODO: No longer needed after Maple.\n            else:\n                try:\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_course_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_jump_to_id_urls(explanation)\n                except (TypeError, AttributeError):\n                    logger.debug('Unable to perform URL substitution on the explanation: %s', explanation)\n\n            answer['explanation'] = explanation\n        return answer\n", "code_after": "    def show_answer(self, data, suffix=''):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns correct answer in assessment mode.\n\n        Raises:\n             * JsonHandlerError with 400 error code in standard mode.\n             * JsonHandlerError with 409 error code if the answer is unavailable.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.mode != Constants.ASSESSMENT_MODE:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                400,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"show_answer handler should only be called for assessment mode\")\n            )\n        if not self.is_answer_available:\n            raise JsonHandlerError(\n                409,\n                self.i18n_service.gettext(\"The answer is unavailable\")\n            )\n\n        answer = self._get_correct_state()\n\n        if explanation := self.data.get('explanation', '').strip():\n            if replace_urls_service := self.runtime.service(self, 'replace_urls'):\n                explanation = replace_urls_service.replace_urls(explanation)\n\n            # pylint: disable=fixme\n            # TODO: No longer needed after Maple.\n            else:\n                try:\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_course_urls(explanation)\n                    explanation = self.runtime.replace_jump_to_id_urls(explanation)\n                except (TypeError, AttributeError):\n                    logger.debug('Unable to perform URL substitution on the explanation: %s', explanation)\n\n            answer['explanation'] = sanitize_html(explanation)\n        return answer\n"}, {"function_name": "_present_feedback", "code_before": "    def _present_feedback(feedback_messages):\n        \"\"\"\n        Transforms feedback messages into format expected by frontend code\n        \"\"\"\n        return [\n            {\"message\": msg.message, \"message_class\": msg.message_class}\n            for msg in feedback_messages\n            if msg.message\n        ]\n", "code_after": "    def _present_feedback(feedback_messages):\n        \"\"\"\n        Transforms feedback messages into format expected by frontend code\n        \"\"\"\n        return [\n            {\"message\": sanitize_html(msg.message), \"message_class\": msg.message_class}\n            for msg in feedback_messages\n            if msg.message\n        ]\n"}, {"function_name": "student_view_data.items_without_answers", "code_before": "        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n            return items\n", "code_after": "        def items_without_answers():\n            \"\"\"\n            Removes feedback and answer from items\n            \"\"\"\n            items = copy.deepcopy(self.data.get('items', ''))\n            for item in items:\n                del item['feedback']\n                # Use item.pop to remove both `item['zone']` and `item['zones']`; we don't have\n                # a guarantee that either will be present, so we can't use `del`. Legacy instances\n                # will have `item['zone']`, while current versions will have `item['zones']`.\n                item.pop('zone', None)\n                item.pop('zones', None)\n                # Fall back on \"backgroundImage\" to be backward-compatible.\n                image_url = item.get('imageURL') or item.get('backgroundImage')\n                if image_url:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = self._expand_static_url(image_url)\n                else:\n                    item['expandedImageURL'] = ''\n                item['displayName'] = sanitize_html(item.get('displayName', ''))\n            return items\n"}, {"function_name": "zones", "code_before": "    def zones(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get drop zone data, defined by the author.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert zone data from old to new format if necessary\n        migrator = StateMigration(self)\n        return [migrator.apply_zone_migrations(zone) for zone in self.data.get('zones', [])]\n", "code_after": "    def zones(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Get drop zone data, defined by the author.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert zone data from old to new format if necessary\n        migrator = StateMigration(self)\n        migrated_zones = []\n\n        for zone in self.data.get('zones', []):\n            result = migrator.apply_zone_migrations(zone)\n            result['title'] = sanitize_html(result.get('title', ''))\n            migrated_zones.append(result)\n\n        return migrated_zones\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `student_view_data` has been modified to sanitize HTML tags to prevent XSS vulnerabilities. The change in the function is the addition of the `sanitize_html` function to sanitize the `displayName` of each item and the `display_name` of the student view data.\n\nThe vulnerability description states that there was an XSS vulnerability in multiple XBlock Fields, and any platform that has deployed the XBlock would be impacted. The commit message also mentions that disallowed HTML tags (e.g., `<script>`) will no longer be rendered in LMS and Studio, which is a common way to prevent XSS attacks.\n\nGiven this information, it can be inferred that the `student_view_data` function was vulnerable to XSS attacks and has been modified to fix this vulnerability. Therefore, the answer is 1.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
