{"function_name": "_iter_extra_field_names", "code_before": "    def _iter_extra_field_names(self) -> Iterator[tuple[str, str]]:\n        \"\"\"Iterate through provider-backed connection fields.\n\n        Note that this cannot be a property (including a cached property)\n        because Flask-Appbuilder attempts to access all members on startup, and\n        using a property would initialize the providers manager too eagerly.\n        \"\"\"\n        return ((k, v.field_name) for k, v in ProvidersManager().connection_form_widgets.items())\n", "code_after": "", "commit_message": "Hide sensitive values from extra in connection edit form (#32309)\n\nThe fields that are sensitive (i.e password field is used\r\nto show them in Connection edit view) should also be hidden\r\nwhen they are stored as \"extra\" in the form extra field.\r\n\r\nThis PR handles both - replacing such values with a\r\nplaceholder as well as not updating the value if the\r\nplaceholder has not been modified.", "commit": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/commit/d01248382fe45a5f5a7fdeed4082a80c5f814ad8", "description": "Apache Airflow, versions before 2.6.3, is affected by a vulnerability that allows an unauthorized actor to gain access to sensitive information in Connection edit view. This vulnerability is considered low since it requires someone with access to Connection resources specifically updating the connection to exploit it. Users should upgrade to version 2.6.3 or later which has removed the vulnerability.\n", "file_change_id": 191405489552995, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xvw9-3mhm-xjqq", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "add_columns", "code_before": "    def add_columns(self) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"A list of columns to show in the Add form.\n\n        This dynamically calculates additional fields from providers and add\n        them to the backing list. This calculation is done exactly once (by\n    