changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "_get_object_element", "code_before": "def _get_object_element(dataset, seq_no, rel_path, download_link):\n    \"\"\"If rel_path and download_link are not None, we are called from scope.\n    Otherwise we are called from ID and need to run SQL query to fetch these attrs.\"\"\"\n\n    if rel_path is None:\n        query = \"SELECT rel_path, download_link FROM \" + \\\n        dataset + \\\n        \" WHERE sequence_no = %s\"\n\n        cnx = mysql.connector.connect(user=DB_USER,\n                                    password=DB_PASSWORD,\n                                    host=DB_HOST,\n                                    database=DB_DBNAME,\n                                    port=DB_PORT)\n        cursor = cnx.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(query, (seq_no,))\n\n        row = cursor.fetchone()\n\n        if not row:\n            return None\n\n        rel_path, download_link = row[0], row[1]\n\n    if LOCAL_OBJ_URI:\n        src_uri = 'file://' + os.path.join(DATAROOT, dataset, rel_path)\n    else:\n        src_uri = url_for('.get_object_src_http', dataset=dataset, rel_path=rel_path)\n\n    return '<object id={} src={} hyperfind.external-link={} />' \\\n        .format(\n        quoteattr(url_for('.get_object_id', dataset=dataset, seq_no=seq_no)),\n        quoteattr(src_uri),\n        quoteattr(download_link))\n", "code_after": "def _get_object_element(dataset, seq_no, rel_path, download_link):\n    \"\"\"If rel_path and download_link are not None, we are called from scope.\n    Otherwise we are called from ID and need to run SQL query to fetch these attrs.\"\"\"\n\n    if rel_path is None:\n        query = \"SELECT rel_path, download_link FROM \" + \\\n        dataset + \\\n        \" WHERE sequence_no = %s\"\n\n        cnx = mysql.connector.connect(user=DB_USER,\n                                    password=DB_PASSWORD,\n                                    host=DB_HOST,\n                                    database=DB_DBNAME,\n                                    port=DB_PORT)\n        cursor = cnx.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(query, (seq_no,))\n\n        row = cursor.fetchone()\n\n        if not row:\n            return None\n\n        rel_path, download_link = row[0], row[1]\n\n    if LOCAL_OBJ_URI:\n        src_uri = 'file://' + _get_obj_absolute_path(dataset, rel_path)\n    else:\n        src_uri = url_for('.get_object_src_http', dataset=dataset, rel_path=rel_path)\n\n    return '<object id={} src={} hyperfind.external-link={} />' \\\n        .format(\n        quoteattr(url_for('.get_object_id', dataset=dataset, seq_no=seq_no)),\n        quoteattr(src_uri),\n        quoteattr(download_link))\n", "commit_message": "Fix path traversal issues in all dataretriever backends", "commit": "https://github.com/cmusatyalab/opendiamond/commit/398049c187ee644beabab44d6fece82251c1ea56", "description": "The cmusatyalab/opendiamond repository through 10.1.1 on GitHub allows absolute path traversal because the Flask send_file function is used unsafely. A patch is available on the `master` branch of the repository.", "file_change_id": 85493540041570, "report_link": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x2pc-fqrw-hc7f", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "_get_obj_abosolute_path", "code_before": "def _get_obj_abosolute_path(dataset, rel_path):\n    return os.path.join(DATAROOT, dataset, rel_path)\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "get_object_src_http", "code_before": "def get_object_src_http(dataset, rel_path):\n    path = _get_obj_abosolute_path(dataset, rel_path)\n    response = send_file(path,\n                         cache_timeout=datetime.timedelta(\n                             days=365).total_seconds(),\n                         add_etags=True,\n                         conditional=True)\n    return response\n", "code_after": "def get_object_src_http(dataset, rel_path):\n    path = _get_obj_absolute_path(dataset, rel_path)\n    response = send_file(path,\n                         cache_timeout=datetime.timedelta(\n                             days=365).total_seconds(),\n                         add_etags=True,\n                         conditional=True)\n    return response\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `_get_object_element` was changed as part of a commit to fix a path traversal vulnerability. The change in the function is related to how the `src_uri` is constructed when `LOCAL_OBJ_URI` is true. In the updated code, the function `_get_obj_absolute_path` is used to get the absolute path of the object.\n\nThe vulnerability description mentions that the issue was due to the unsafe use of the Flask `send_file` function, which allows absolute path traversal. The function `_get_obj_absolute_path` was removed in the same commit, and it seems like it was used to construct absolute paths. This suggests that the changes in `_get_object_element` are directly related to the vulnerability.\n\nTherefore, the function `_get_object_element` appears to be vulnerable and was changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
