  # We disable auto_decompress when forward / proxy log url.\n        self._proxy_session = aiohttp.ClientSession(auto_decompress=False)\n        log_utils.register_mimetypes()\n        routes.static(\"/logs\", self._dashboard_head.log_dir, show_index=True)\n        GlobalSignals.node_info_fetched.append(self.insert_log_url_to_node_info)\n        GlobalSignals.node_summary_fetched.append(self.insert_log_url_to_node_info)\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "run", "code_before": "    async def run(self, server):\n        pass\n", "code_after": ""}], "gpt_answer": "The vulnerability described allows attackers to remotely read any file on the system depending on the permissions of the user that started Ray. The function `get_log_index` is removed in the commit, which is part of the fix to the vulnerability. The function was responsible for creating a list of log URLs for each node, which could potentially be exploited to read any file on the system.\n\nThe commit message also mentions that the log_proxy API is being removed due to some security issues, which further supports the idea that this function was part of the vulnerability.\n\nTherefore, the function `get_log_index` is relevant to the vulnerability that the commit is trying to fix.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "__init__", "code_before": "    def __init__(self, dashboard_head):\n        super().__init__(dashboard_head)\n        # We disable auto_decompress when forward / proxy log url.\n        self._proxy_session = aiohttp.ClientSession(auto_decompress=False)\n        log_utils.register_mimetypes()\n        routes.static(\"/logs\", self._dashboard_head.log_dir, show_index=True)\n        GlobalSignals.node_info_fetched.append(self.insert_log_url_to_node_info)\n        GlobalSignals.node_summary_fetched.append(self.insert_log_url_to_node_info)\n", "code_after": "", "commit_message": "[Dashboard] Migrate Logs page to use state api. (#41474)\n\nMigrates to use state-api, to unify behavior with CLI and UI\r\nDelete log_proxy API, it's legacy and has some security issues.\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\nSigned-off-by: Alan Guo <aguo@anyscale.com>", "commit": "https://github.com/ray-project/ray/commit/2a6c6ee032701e49bcebd1df1a400f70fddb0cc7", "description": "Description\nAttackers can read any file on the system with the permissions of the user that started the Ray Dashboard.\nProof of Concept\nGET /api/v0/logs/file?node_id=56424ecdb00cf570f0831aa698dd7c44e527a20212d2fa27078c7f79&filename=../../../../../etc%2fpasswd&lines=50000 HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8265\nUser-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.15; rv:109.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/114.0\nAccept: application/json, text/plain, */*\nAccept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.5\nAccept-Encoding: gzip, deflate\nConnection: close\nReferer: http://localhost:8265/\nSec-Fetch-Dest: empty\nSec-Fetch-Mode: cors\nSec-Fetch-Site: same-origin\n\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nContent-Type: text/plain\nDate: Thu, 24 Aug 2023 21:49:54 GMT\nServer: Python/3.8 aiohttp/3.8.5\nConnection: close\nContent-Length: 8225\n\n1##\n# User Database\n# \n# Note that this file is consulted directly only when the system is running\n# in single-user mode.  At other times this information is provided by\n# Open Directory.\n#\n# See the opendirectoryd(8) man page for additional information about\n# Open Directory.\n##\nnobody:*:-2:-2:Unprivileged User:/var/empty:/usr/bin/false\nroot:*:0:0:System Administrator:/var/root:/bin/sh\ndaemon:*:1:1:System Services:/var/root:/usr/bin/false\nfakeuser:*:99:99:Fake User:/Users/danmcinerney/fakeuser:/bin/sh\n_uucp:*:4:4:Unix to Unix Copy Protocol:/var/spool/uucp:/usr/sbin/uucico\nImpact\nAllows attackers to remotely read any file on the system depending on the permissions of the user that started Ray.", "file_change_id": 180097786126833, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/5039c045-f986-4cbc-81ac-370fe4b0d3f8/", "programming_language": "unknown", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "insert_log_url_to_node_info", "code_before": "    async def insert_log_url_to_node_info(self, node_info):\n        node_id = node_info.get(\"raylet\", {}).get(\"nodeId\")\n        if node_id is None:\n            return\n        agent_port = DataSource.agents.get(node_id)\n        if agent_port is None:\n            return\n        agent_http_port, _ = agent_port\n        log_url = self.LOG_URL_TEMPLATE.format(\n            ip=node_info.get(\"ip\"), port=agent_http_port\n        )\n        node_info[\"logUrl\"] = log_url\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "_directory_as_html", "code_before": "    def _directory_as_html(index_text_log_url) -> str:\n        # returns directory's index as html\n\n        index_of = \"Index of logs\"\n        h1 = f\"<h1>{index_of}</h1>\"\n\n        index_list = []\n        for text, log_url in index_text_log_url:\n            index_list.append(f'<li><a href=\"{log_url}\">{text}</a></li>')\n        index_list = \"\\n\".join(index_list)\n        ul = f\"<ul>\\n{index_list}\\n</ul>\"\n        body = f\"<body>\\n{h1}\\n{ul}\\n</body>\"\n\n        head_str = f\"<head>\\n<title>{index_of}</title>\\n</head>\"\n        html = f\"<html>\\n{head_str}\\n{body}\\n</html>\"\n\n        return html\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "get_log_from_proxy", "code_before": "    async def get_log_from_proxy(self, req) -> aiohttp.web.StreamResponse:\n        url = req.query.get(\"url\")\n        if not url:\n            raise Exception(\"url is None.\")\n        body = await req.read()\n        # Special logic to handle hashtags only. The only character that\n        # is not getting properly encoded by aiohttp's static file server\n        encoded_url = url.replace(\"#\", \"%23\")\n        async with self._proxy_session.request(\n            req.method, encoded_url, data=body, headers=req.headers\n        ) as r:\n            sr = aiohttp.web.StreamResponse(\n                status=r.status, reason=r.reason, headers=req.headers\n            )\n            sr.content_length = r.content_length\n            sr.content_type = r.content_type\n            if r.charset and not sr.content_type.startswith(\"application/octet-stream\"):\n                sr.charset = r.charset\n            writer = await sr.prepare(req)\n            async for data in r.content.iter_any():\n                await writer.write(data)\n\n            return sr\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "get_log_index", "code_before": "    async def get_log_index(self, req) -> aiohttp.web.Response:\n        agent_ips = set()\n        index_text_log_url = []\n        for node_id, ports in DataSource.agents.items():\n            ip = DataSource.node_id_to_ip[node_id]\n            agent_ips.add(ip)\n            # Use node_id(ip) as log url's text\n            index_text = self.LOG_INDEX_TEXT_TEMPLATE.format(\n                node_id=node_id, node_ip=ip\n            )\n            log_url = self.LOG_URL_TEMPLATE.format(ip=ip, port=str(ports[0]))\n            index_text_log_url.append((index_text, log_url))\n        if self._dashboard_head.ip not in agent_ips:\n            index_text = self.LOG_INDEX_TEXT_TEMPLATE.format(\n                node_id=\"head\", node_ip=self._dashboard_head.ip\n            )\n            log_url = self.LOG_URL_TEMPLATE.format(\n                ip=self._dashboard_head.ip, port=self._dashboard_head.http_port\n            )\n            index_text_log_url.append((index_text, log_url))\n        return aiohttp.web.Response(\n            text=self._directory_as_html(index_text_log_url), content_type=\"text/html\"\n        )\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "is_minimal_module", "code_before": "    def is_minimal_module():\n        return False\n", "code_after": ""}, {"function_name": "run", "code_before": "    async def run(self, server):\n        pass\n", "code_after": ""}], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the vulnerability allowed attackers to read any file on the system with the permissions of the user that started the Ray Dashboard. The commit message suggests that the commit is intended to migrate the Logs page to use the state API and delete the log_proxy API, which is described as legacy and having some security issues.\n\nThe \"__init__\" function in the \"before\" code creates a new aiohttp.ClientSession with auto_decompress set to False, and adds some handlers. In the \"after\" code, this function is completely removed.\n\nGiven the vulnerability description and the changes made in the commit, it seems that the \"__init__\" function was part of the vulnerable code (it created the aiohttp.ClientSession that might have been used in the vulnerable log_proxy API), and it was removed as part of the fix.\n\nTherefore, the \"__init__\" function can be considered as vulnerable.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "clean_identity", "code_before": "    def clean_identity(self):\n        v = self.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        if len(v) > 254:\n            raise forms.ValidationError(\"Address is too long.\")\n\n        if User.objects.filter(email=v).exists():\n            raise forms.ValidationError(\n                \"An account with this email address already exists.\"\n            )\n\n        return v\n", "code_after": "    def clean_identity(self):\n        v = self.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        if not TokenBucket.authorize_login_email(v):\n            raise forms.ValidationError(\"Too many attempts, please try later.\")\n\n        try:\n            self.user = User.objects.get(email=v)\n        except User.DoesNotExist:\n            self.user = None\n\n        return v\n", "commit_message": "Fix login and signup views to make email enumeration harder", "commit": "https://github.com/healthchecks/healthchecks/commit/359edbd2709e27b60687061a32e19322bc971c1f", "description": "Description\nThe sending a magic sign in link functionality is vulnerable to an email enumeration attack.\nProof of Concept\nIf you enter registered email, you will get Login Link Sent! message.\nIf you enter non-registered email, you will get Unknown email address. message.\nImpact\nEmail enumeration allows an attacker to find valid usernames/emails on the victim application. It can use this information to do more advanced attacks like bruteforcing passwords or phishing attemps.", "file_change_id": 18128437869684, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/208a096f-7986-4eed-8629-b7285348a686/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function \"clean_identity\" was changed to mitigate a vulnerability that allowed email enumeration. The vulnerability allowed an attacker to determine if an email was registered with the service based on the response message.\n\nIn the \"code_before\" snippet, the function checks if a user with the provided email exists and raises a ValidationError if it does. This is the behavior that allowed email enumeration.\n\nIn the \"code_after\" snippet, the function has been changed to use the \"TokenBucket.authorize_login_email(v)\" method. If the method returns False, a ValidationError is raised with a generic \"Too many attempts, please try later.\" message. This change makes it harder for an attacker to determine if an email is registered with the service based on the response message.\n\nTherefore, the function \"clean_identity\" was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "login", "code_before": "def login(request):\n    form = forms.PasswordLoginForm()\n    magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm()\n\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        if request.POST.get(\"action\") == \"login\":\n            form = forms.PasswordLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if form.is_valid():\n                return _check_2fa(request, form.user)\n\n        else:\n            magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if magic_form.is_valid():\n                redirect_url = request.GET.get(\"next\")\n                if not _allow_redirect(redirect_url):\n                    redirect_url = None\n\n                profile = Profile.objects.for_user(magic_form.user)\n                profile.send_instant_login_link(redirect_url=redirect_url)\n                response = redirect(\"hc-login-link-sent\")\n\n                # check_token looks for this cookie to decide if\n                # it needs to do the extra POST step.\n                response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n                return response\n\n    if request.user.is_authenticated:\n        return _redirect_after_login(request)\n\n    bad_link = request.session.pop(\"bad_link\", None)\n    ctx = {\n        \"page\": \"login\",\n        \"form\": form,\n        \"magic_form\": magic_form,\n        \"bad_link\": bad_link,\n        \"registration_open\": settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN,\n        \"support_email\": settings.SUPPORT_EMAIL,\n    }\n    return render(request, \"accounts/login.html\", ctx)\n", "code_after": "def login(request):\n    form = forms.PasswordLoginForm()\n    magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm()\n\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        if request.POST.get(\"action\") == \"login\":\n            form = forms.PasswordLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if form.is_valid():\n                return _check_2fa(request, form.user)\n\n        else:\n            magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if magic_form.is_valid():\n                redirect_url = request.GET.get(\"next\")\n                if not _allow_redirect(redirect_url):\n                    redirect_url = None\n\n                if magic_form.user:\n                    profile = Profile.objects.for_user(magic_form.user)\n                    profile.send_instant_login_link(redirect_url=redirect_url)\n\n                response = redirect(\"hc-login-link-sent\")\n                # check_token looks for this cookie to decide if\n                # it needs to do the extra POST step.\n                response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n                return response\n\n    if request.user.is_authenticated:\n        return _redirect_after_login(request)\n\n    bad_link = request.session.pop(\"bad_link\", None)\n    ctx = {\n        \"page\": \"login\",\n        \"form\": form,\n        \"magic_form\": magic_form,\n        \"bad_link\": bad_link,\n        \"registration_open\": settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN,\n        \"support_email\": settings.SUPPORT_EMAIL,\n    }\n    return render(request, \"accounts/login.html\", ctx)\n", "commit_message": "Fix login and signup views to make email enumeration harder", "commit": "https://github.com/healthchecks/healthchecks/commit/359edbd2709e27b60687061a32e19322bc971c1f", "description": "Description\nThe sending a magic sign in link functionality is vulnerable to an email enumeration attack.\nProof of Concept\nIf you enter registered email, you will get Login Link Sent! message.\nIf you enter non-registered email, you will get Unknown email address. message.\nImpact\nEmail enumeration allows an attacker to find valid usernames/emails on the victim application. It can use this information to do more advanced attacks like bruteforcing passwords or phishing attemps.", "file_change_id": 85853680291998, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/208a096f-7986-4eed-8629-b7285348a686/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "signup", "code_before": "def signup(request):\n    if not settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden()\n\n    ctx = {}\n    form = forms.SignupForm(request.POST)\n    if form.is_valid():\n        email = form.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        tz = form.cleaned_data[\"tz\"]\n        user = _make_user(email, tz)\n        profile = Profile.objects.for_user(user)\n        profile.send_instant_login_link()\n        ctx[\"created\"] = True\n    else:\n        ctx = {\"form\": form}\n\n    response = render(request, \"accounts/signup_result.html\", ctx)\n    if ctx.get(\"created\"):\n        response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n\n    return response\n", "code_after": "def signup(request):\n    if not settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden()\n\n    ctx = {}\n    form = forms.SignupForm(request.POST)\n    if form.is_valid():\n        email = form.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        if not User.objects.filter(email=email).exists():\n            tz = form.cleaned_data[\"tz\"]\n            user = _make_user(email, tz)\n            profile = Profile.objects.for_user(user)\n            profile.send_instant_login_link()\n    else:\n        ctx = {\"form\": form}\n\n    response = render(request, \"accounts/signup_result.html\", ctx)\n    if \"form\" not in ctx:\n        response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n\n    return response\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The vulnerability described is an email enumeration attack, where the application reveals whether an email is registered or not. This can be exploited by attackers to gather valid emails for further attacks.\n\nIn the \"login\" function, the change made is the addition of a condition to check if the user exists before sending the instant login link. This change is directly related to the vulnerability, as it prevents the application from revealing whether an email is registered or not. If the user does not exist, the application will not send an instant login link, thus not revealing the existence or non-existence of the user.\n\nTherefore, the function was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "signup", "code_before": "def signup(request):\n    if not settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden()\n\n    ctx = {}\n    form = forms.SignupForm(request.POST)\n    if form.is_valid():\n        email = form.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        tz = form.cleaned_data[\"tz\"]\n        user = _make_user(email, tz)\n        profile = Profile.objects.for_user(user)\n        profile.send_instant_login_link()\n        ctx[\"created\"] = True\n    else:\n        ctx = {\"form\": form}\n\n    response = render(request, \"accounts/signup_result.html\", ctx)\n    if ctx.get(\"created\"):\n        response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n\n    return response\n", "code_after": "def signup(request):\n    if not settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden()\n\n    ctx = {}\n    form = forms.SignupForm(request.POST)\n    if form.is_valid():\n        email = form.cleaned_data[\"identity\"]\n        if not User.objects.filter(email=email).exists():\n            tz = form.cleaned_data[\"tz\"]\n            user = _make_user(email, tz)\n            profile = Profile.objects.for_user(user)\n            profile.send_instant_login_link()\n    else:\n        ctx = {\"form\": form}\n\n    response = render(request, \"accounts/signup_result.html\", ctx)\n    if \"form\" not in ctx:\n        response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n\n    return response\n", "commit_message": "Fix login and signup views to make email enumeration harder", "commit": "https://github.com/healthchecks/healthchecks/commit/359edbd2709e27b60687061a32e19322bc971c1f", "description": "Description\nThe sending a magic sign in link functionality is vulnerable to an email enumeration attack.\nProof of Concept\nIf you enter registered email, you will get Login Link Sent! message.\nIf you enter non-registered email, you will get Unknown email address. message.\nImpact\nEmail enumeration allows an attacker to find valid usernames/emails on the victim application. It can use this information to do more advanced attacks like bruteforcing passwords or phishing attemps.", "file_change_id": 85853680291998, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/208a096f-7986-4eed-8629-b7285348a686/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "login", "code_before": "def login(request):\n    form = forms.PasswordLoginForm()\n    magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm()\n\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        if request.POST.get(\"action\") == \"login\":\n            form = forms.PasswordLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if form.is_valid():\n                return _check_2fa(request, form.user)\n\n        else:\n            magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if magic_form.is_valid():\n                redirect_url = request.GET.get(\"next\")\n                if not _allow_redirect(redirect_url):\n                    redirect_url = None\n\n                profile = Profile.objects.for_user(magic_form.user)\n                profile.send_instant_login_link(redirect_url=redirect_url)\n                response = redirect(\"hc-login-link-sent\")\n\n                # check_token looks for this cookie to decide if\n                # it needs to do the extra POST step.\n                response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n                return response\n\n    if request.user.is_authenticated:\n        return _redirect_after_login(request)\n\n    bad_link = request.session.pop(\"bad_link\", None)\n    ctx = {\n        \"page\": \"login\",\n        \"form\": form,\n        \"magic_form\": magic_form,\n        \"bad_link\": bad_link,\n        \"registration_open\": settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN,\n        \"support_email\": settings.SUPPORT_EMAIL,\n    }\n    return render(request, \"accounts/login.html\", ctx)\n", "code_after": "def login(request):\n    form = forms.PasswordLoginForm()\n    magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm()\n\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        if request.POST.get(\"action\") == \"login\":\n            form = forms.PasswordLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if form.is_valid():\n                return _check_2fa(request, form.user)\n\n        else:\n            magic_form = forms.EmailLoginForm(request.POST)\n            if magic_form.is_valid():\n                redirect_url = request.GET.get(\"next\")\n                if not _allow_redirect(redirect_url):\n                    redirect_url = None\n\n                if magic_form.user:\n                    profile = Profile.objects.for_user(magic_form.user)\n                    profile.send_instant_login_link(redirect_url=redirect_url)\n\n                response = redirect(\"hc-login-link-sent\")\n                # check_token looks for this cookie to decide if\n                # it needs to do the extra POST step.\n                response.set_cookie(\"auto-login\", \"1\", max_age=300, httponly=True)\n                return response\n\n    if request.user.is_authenticated:\n        return _redirect_after_login(request)\n\n    bad_link = request.session.pop(\"bad_link\", None)\n    ctx = {\n        \"page\": \"login\",\n        \"form\": form,\n        \"magic_form\": magic_form,\n        \"bad_link\": bad_link,\n        \"registration_open\": settings.REGISTRATION_OPEN,\n        \"support_email\": settings.SUPPORT_EMAIL,\n    }\n    return render(request, \"accounts/login.html\", ctx)\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The vulnerability described is an email enumeration attack, where the application reveals whether an email is registered or not. This can be used by an attacker to gather valid emails for further attacks.\n\nLooking at the changes in the `signup` function, we can see that the code has been modified to check if a user with the provided email already exists before proceeding with the signup process. This change is directly related to the described vulnerability, as it prevents the application from revealing whether an email is already registered or not.\n\nTherefore, the `signup` function was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "has_numeric_only", "code_before": "    def has_numeric_only(self, text):\n        return bool(re.search(r\"(.*)[\\s]+(\\#NUMERIC_ONLY\\#)\", text))\n", "code_after": "    def has_numeric_only(self, text):\n        return bool(re.search(r\"[\\s]+(\\#NUMERIC_ONLY\\#)\", text))\n", "commit_message": "patching cve", "commit": "https://github.com/alvations/sacremoses/commit/8ad457e3cc25579140757befffd6f0e3b421728d", "description": "\u270d\ufe0f Description\nThe sacremoses package is vulnerable to ReDoS (regular expression denial of service). An attacker that is able to provide a crafted text as input to the has_numeric_only function may cause an application to consume an excessive amount of CPU. Below pinned line using vulnerable regex.\n\ud83d\udd75\ufe0f\u200d\u2642\ufe0f Proof of Concept\nReproducer where we\u2019ve copied the relevant code:\nhttps://github.com/alvations/sacremoses/blob/dc203fb2b41e1f8c8bbbd4606732945e6cdb090e/sacremoses/tokenize.py#L366\nPut the below in a poc.py file and run\nimport time\nimport re\n\ndef has_numeric_only(text):\n        return bool(re.search(r\"(.*)[\\s]+(\\#NUMERIC_ONLY\\#)\", text))\n\nfor i in range(1, 50000):\n    start_time = time.perf_counter()\n    payload = \" \" + \" \" * (i*500) + \"\"\n    has_numeric_only(payload)\n    stop_time = time.perf_counter() - start_time\n    print(\"Payload.length: \" + str(len(payload)) + \": \" + str(stop_time) + \" ms\")\nCheck the Output:\nPayload.length: 501: 0.2941443 ms\nPayload.length: 1001: 2.5347709000000003 ms\nPayload.length: 1501: 9.3377153 ms\nPayload.length: 2001: 21.428344199999998 ms\nPayload.length: 2501: 40.7420754 ms\n--\n--\n\ud83d\udca5 Impact\nThis vulnerability is capable of exhausting system resources and leads to crashes.", "file_change_id": 234411309062921, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/15d563b2-ce1c-4757-996c-bdf340f2e4ec/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function \"has_numeric_only\" was indeed vulnerable to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) attack. The vulnerability was due to the use of a regular expression that could lead to excessive CPU usage when processing crafted input.\n\nThe change in the function is directly related to the regular expression used. The original regular expression `r\"(.*)[\\s]+(\\#NUMERIC_ONLY\\#)\"` was changed to `r\"[\\s]+(\\#NUMERIC_ONLY\\#)\"`. This change removes the greedy capture group `(.*)` which was causing the ReDoS vulnerability.\n\nGiven the description of the vulnerability and the changes made to the function, it is clear that the function \"has_numeric_only\" was vulnerable and the changes were made to fix this vulnerability.\n\nSo, the answer is 1 (the function is vulnerable).\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "validate_emails", "code_before": "    def validate_emails(self, field):\n        for email in [email.strip() for email in self.emails.data.split(\",\")]:\n            try:\n                email_validator.validate_email(email)\n            except email_validator.EmailNotValidError:\n                raise ValidationError(\n                    _(\"The email %(email)s is not valid\", email=email)\n                )\n", "code_after": "    def validate_emails(self, field):\n        for email in [email.strip() for email in self.emails.data.split(\",\")]:\n            try:\n                email_validator.validate_email(email)\n            except email_validator.EmailNotValidError:\n                raise ValidationError(\n                    _(\"The email %(email)s is not valid\", email=em_surround(email))\n                )\n", "commit_message": "Surround email in case of error (#1044)\n\nfix https://huntr.dev/bounties/441cc44c-6837-46ec-9b30-52455aa71a2f/", "commit": "https://github.com/spiral-project/ihatemoney/commit/667b65b9ccb5c68c2f251be12d6aa3d06cdcb0ba", "description": "Description\nihatemoney is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) when inviting people via email.\nSteps to reproduce\n1.Go to https://ihatemoney.org/ and try out the demo.\n2.In the bottom left, click on Invite people.\n3.In the Send via Emails section, input the payload: <img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)> into the People to notify field.\n4.Click the Send the invitations button and you will see that a pop-up will display.\nImpact\nThis vulnerability has the potential to deface websites, result in compromised user accounts, and can run malicious code on web pages, which can lead to a compromise of the user\u2019s device.", "file_change_id": 61270805390466, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/441cc44c-6837-46ec-9b30-52455aa71a2f/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [], "gpt_answer": "The provided information indicates that the function `validate_emails` was changed to address a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability. The vulnerability was that when inviting people via email, an attacker could input a payload that would execute malicious code when the invitation was sent.\n\nThe change in the function is the addition of `em_surround(email)` in the ValidationError message. This change is likely to sanitize the email input to prevent the execution of any malicious code that might be included in it.\n\nGiven this, it can be concluded that the function `validate_emails` was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "archive", "code_before": "def archive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    archive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def archive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    archive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "commit_message": "Fix bookmark access restrictions", "commit": "https://github.com/sissbruecker/linkding/commit/1ffc3e02667b4218b6d39c36f9cbdfe8418dd2d0", "description": "Description\nThere are multiple idors i found. In bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/edit, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/remove, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/archive, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/unarchive. It gets the object provided in the bookmark_id without checking if the owner of the object is the current user.\nProof of Concept\n1. Go to https://demo.linkding.link/bookmarks/5/remove\n2. The bookmark id 5 will be removed even if you dont own the bookmark. \nImpact\nIdor", "file_change_id": 213048170349231, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/f41645ff-c2a9-4920-a61e-915f890a7229/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "edit", "code_before": "def edit(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n\n    if request.method == 'POST':\n        form = BookmarkForm(request.POST, instance=bookmark)\n        return_url = form.data['return_url']\n        if form.is_valid():\n            tag_string = convert_tag_string(form.data['tag_string'])\n            update_bookmark(form.save(commit=False), tag_string, request.user)\n            return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n    else:\n        return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n        form = BookmarkForm(instance=bookmark)\n\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n\n    form.initial['tag_string'] = build_tag_string(bookmark.tag_names, ' ')\n    form.initial['return_url'] = return_url\n\n    context = {\n        'form': form,\n        'bookmark_id': bookmark_id,\n        'return_url': return_url\n    }\n\n    return render(request, 'bookmarks/edit.html', context)\n", "code_after": "def edit(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    if request.method == 'POST':\n        form = BookmarkForm(request.POST, instance=bookmark)\n        return_url = form.data['return_url']\n        if form.is_valid():\n            tag_string = convert_tag_string(form.data['tag_string'])\n            update_bookmark(form.save(commit=False), tag_string, request.user)\n            return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n    else:\n        return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n        form = BookmarkForm(instance=bookmark)\n\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n\n    form.initial['tag_string'] = build_tag_string(bookmark.tag_names, ' ')\n    form.initial['return_url'] = return_url\n\n    context = {\n        'form': form,\n        'bookmark_id': bookmark_id,\n        'return_url': return_url\n    }\n\n    return render(request, 'bookmarks/edit.html', context)\n"}, {"function_name": "unarchive", "code_before": "def unarchive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    unarchive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:archived')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def unarchive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    unarchive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:archived')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n"}, {"function_name": "remove", "code_before": "def remove(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    bookmark.delete()\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def remove(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    bookmark.delete()\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The vulnerability described in the advisory is an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This type of vulnerability occurs when an application provides direct access to objects based on user-supplied input. In this case, the application was allowing users to access bookmarks by their ID without checking if the user is the owner of the bookmark.\n\nLooking at the changes in the \"archive\" function, it's clear that the function was vulnerable to the IDOR vulnerability. In the \"before\" code, the function was fetching a bookmark based on the ID supplied in the request without checking if the user making the request is the owner of the bookmark. In the \"after\" code, the function has been modified to fetch the bookmark based on both the ID and the owner. If the bookmark does not exist or the user is not the owner, an HTTP 404 error is raised.\n\nTherefore, the \"archive\" function was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
{"function_name": "edit", "code_before": "def edit(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n\n    if request.method == 'POST':\n        form = BookmarkForm(request.POST, instance=bookmark)\n        return_url = form.data['return_url']\n        if form.is_valid():\n            tag_string = convert_tag_string(form.data['tag_string'])\n            update_bookmark(form.save(commit=False), tag_string, request.user)\n            return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n    else:\n        return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n        form = BookmarkForm(instance=bookmark)\n\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n\n    form.initial['tag_string'] = build_tag_string(bookmark.tag_names, ' ')\n    form.initial['return_url'] = return_url\n\n    context = {\n        'form': form,\n        'bookmark_id': bookmark_id,\n        'return_url': return_url\n    }\n\n    return render(request, 'bookmarks/edit.html', context)\n", "code_after": "def edit(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    if request.method == 'POST':\n        form = BookmarkForm(request.POST, instance=bookmark)\n        return_url = form.data['return_url']\n        if form.is_valid():\n            tag_string = convert_tag_string(form.data['tag_string'])\n            update_bookmark(form.save(commit=False), tag_string, request.user)\n            return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n    else:\n        return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n        form = BookmarkForm(instance=bookmark)\n\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n\n    form.initial['tag_string'] = build_tag_string(bookmark.tag_names, ' ')\n    form.initial['return_url'] = return_url\n\n    context = {\n        'form': form,\n        'bookmark_id': bookmark_id,\n        'return_url': return_url\n    }\n\n    return render(request, 'bookmarks/edit.html', context)\n", "commit_message": "Fix bookmark access restrictions", "commit": "https://github.com/sissbruecker/linkding/commit/1ffc3e02667b4218b6d39c36f9cbdfe8418dd2d0", "description": "Description\nThere are multiple idors i found. In bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/edit, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/remove, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/archive, bookmarks/<int:bookmark_id>/unarchive. It gets the object provided in the bookmark_id without checking if the owner of the object is the current user.\nProof of Concept\n1. Go to https://demo.linkding.link/bookmarks/5/remove\n2. The bookmark id 5 will be removed even if you dont own the bookmark. \nImpact\nIdor", "file_change_id": 213048170349231, "report_link": "https://huntr.com/bounties/f41645ff-c2a9-4920-a61e-915f890a7229/", "programming_language": "Python", "other_changed_function_in_the_commit": [{"function_name": "archive", "code_before": "def archive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    archive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def archive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    archive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n"}, {"function_name": "unarchive", "code_before": "def unarchive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    unarchive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:archived')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def unarchive(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    unarchive_bookmark(bookmark)\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:archived')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n"}, {"function_name": "remove", "code_before": "def remove(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id)\n    bookmark.delete()\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n", "code_after": "def remove(request, bookmark_id: int):\n    try:\n        bookmark = Bookmark.objects.get(pk=bookmark_id, owner=request.user)\n    except Bookmark.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404('Bookmark does not exist')\n\n    bookmark.delete()\n    return_url = request.GET.get('return_url')\n    return_url = return_url if return_url else reverse('bookmarks:index')\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(return_url)\n"}], "gpt_answer": "The vulnerability described in the advisory is an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This type of vulnerability occurs when an application provides direct access to objects based on user-supplied input. In this case, the application was allowing users to edit, remove, archive, and unarchive bookmarks without checking if the user was the owner of the bookmark.\n\nLooking at the changes made to the \"edit\" function, it's clear that the function was vulnerable. The original code fetched the bookmark based on the bookmark_id without checking if the current user was the owner of the bookmark. The updated code adds a check to ensure that the bookmark being fetched belongs to the current user. If the bookmark does not exist or does not belong to the current user, an Http404 error is raised.\n\nTherefore, the \"edit\" function was vulnerable and has been changed to fix the vulnerability.\n\n```json\n{\n\"answer\": 1\n}\n```"}
